## Use the sine rule in triangle BCD
$|BC|$ is opposite the $42^\circ$ angle, and $|BD| = 16$ is opposite the $110^\circ$ angle.
\frac{|BC|}{\sin 42^\circ} &= \frac{16}{\sin 110^\circ}
## Solve for |BC|
|BC| &= \frac{16 \sin 42^\circ}{\sin 110^\circ}
&= 11.393\ldots
&= 11.39 \text{ m}
ANSWER: |BC| = 11.39 \text{ m}

## Measure |OB| and |OQ|
Measure with a ruler, in cm. The printed triangle has $|AB| = 5$ cm. Any answer within 5 mm is accepted.
|OB| &\approx 15 \text{ cm}
|OQ| &\approx 22.5 \text{ cm}
## Find the scale factor
The scale factor is the image distance divided by the original distance.
k &= \frac{|OQ|}{|OB|}
&= \frac{22.5}{15}
&= 1.5
ANSWER: k = 1.5

## (i) Find |PQ|
Each image length is $k$ times the original length.
|PQ| &= k \times |AB|
&= 1.5 \times 5
&= 7.5 \text{ cm}
## (ii) Find |BC|
Divide the image length by $k$ to get the original length.
|BC| &= \frac{|QR|}{k}
&= \frac{8.7}{1.5}
&= 5.8 \text{ cm}
## (iii) Show the angles are equal using cosines
Both triangles have a right angle ($A$ and $P$), so $\cos$ is adjacent over hypotenuse.
\cos|\angle ABC| &= \frac{|AB|}{|BC|} = \frac{5}{5.8}
\cos|\angle PQR| &= \frac{|PQ|}{|QR|} = \frac{7.5}{8.7}
&= \frac{5}{5.8}
\cos|\angle ABC| &= \cos|\angle PQR|
Both angles are acute, so $|\angle ABC| = |\angle PQR|$.
ANSWER: |PQ| = 7.5 \text{ cm}, \; |BC| = 5.8 \text{ cm}, \; |\angle ABC| = |\angle PQR|

## Halve the diameter
The radius is half the diameter.
r &= \frac{12}{2}
&= 6 \text{ m}
ANSWER: r = 6 \text{ m}

## Divide the area by the coverage of one litre
One litre covers $3.5 \text{ m}^2$, so divide the area by $3.5$.
\text{Litres} &= \frac{452.4}{3.5}
&\approx 129.26
&\approx 129
ANSWER: 129 \text{ litres}

## Use the smallest and largest possible heights
The tallest girl is at most $185$ cm and the shortest is at least $145$ cm.
\text{Range} &= 185 - 145
&= 40 \text{ cm}
ANSWER: 40 \text{ cm}

## Interpret the median
The median is the middle value. Half of the 500 girls (250 girls) are shorter than $164.5$ cm and half are taller.
ANSWER: \text{Half the girls are shorter than } 164.5 \text{ cm}

## Compare the spreads
The girls' standard deviation ($7.7$ cm) is smaller than the boys' ($8.9$ cm), so the girls' heights are less spread out and closer to their mean. The boys' heights vary more.
ANSWER: \text{Girls' heights are less spread out}
